# Bonded topology for the Martini 3.0.0 coarse-grain protein model: which
# springs exist. Generated by data/martini3/prepare_martini3_data.py -- do
# not edit by hand. Use it with -rigidbody, which is exclusive with -cutoff:
# a distance cutoff would invent a network, and the point of this file is
# that Martini's own bonded graph is used instead.
#
# Every group here has exactly TWO atoms, so every group is exactly one
# spring. Pair it with data/reducerules/martini3.grp, whose bead names these
# are.
#
# NO FORCE CONSTANT APPEARS IN THIS FILE and none belongs here: a spring's
# stiffness is a construction input (pdb2spn's -stiffness, stored per spring
# in the .nc, unreachable from the .msp). Martini's own constants, where it
# states any, are in the companion .bi.ff and are read only if -bondstiffness
# is given.
#
# WHAT IS HERE, from martini3001's aminoacids.ff: every side-chain [bonds]
# and [constraints] pair, deduplicated because the two sections declare the
# same pair twice for most side chains (once under 'ifndef FLEXIBLE' and once
# under 'ifdef FLEXIBLE'); the 1-3 pair of every side-chain [angles] entry,
# which is how BioSpring holds an angle; and from the 39 [link] blocks, the
# backbone bond BB-+BB plus the 1-3 pairs of the backbone angles.
#
# WHAT CANNOT BE HERE: 'BB ++BB' and 'BB +++BB', the elastic bonds that
# stabilise extended regions and helices, because RigidBodyBuilder strips ONE
# +/- prefix and moves exactly one residue -- a two-residue offset resolves
# to an atom named '+BB' in the next residue, which does not exist. Four of
# the backbone bond patterns and two of the five dihedral patterns are lost
# that way. Nor is 'SC1 >SC1', the disulfide bridge, which is not between
# neighbours at all: -static-disulfide covers it.
#
# THE SECONDARY-STRUCTURE CHOICE IS ALSO ABSENT, and costs nothing. Martini
# declares three alternative BB-+BB bonds (0.350 / 0.3375 / 0.365 nm) and
# three constraints (0.310 / 0.33 / 0.3375 nm), picked by DSSP; a .rbody keys
# on residue name and chain position, never on secondary structure. But a
# BioSpring spring equilibrates at the distance in the INPUT structure, which
# in a helix already IS 0.310 nm -- the same measurement Martini's table came
# from. And the force constant is 4000 kJ.mol-1.nm-2 on all three bond
# variants, so only the bond-or-constraint distinction varies, which is the
# construction choice above.
#
# TRP SC3 GETS FOUR SPRINGS MARTINI DOES NOT GIVE IT. There it is a virtual
# site placed from SC1/SC2/SC4/SC5 and carries no bonded term at all. Here it
# is a real bead, so with no spring it would be held by nothing but the
# non-bonded terms and would drift out of the ring. It is tied to the four
# beads its virtual-site definition uses.
#
#
M3_A_BB_pBB ALA BB +BB
M3_A_mBB_pBB ALA -BB +BB
M3_A_mBB_SC1 ALA -BB SC1
M3_A_SC1_pBB ALA SC1 +BB
M3_A_BB_SC1 ALA BB SC1
#
M3_C_BB_pBB CYS BB +BB
M3_C_mBB_pBB CYS -BB +BB
M3_C_mBB_SC1 CYS -BB SC1
M3_C_SC1_pBB CYS SC1 +BB
M3_C_BB_SC1 CYS BB SC1
